/-!
# Source reductions for the rank-one local action

The source proves W_K reduced for K₋LᵥTᵥ. We prove that assertion directly
from the Sylow-central seed, keeping the actual plus quotient. We also show
that the whole actor preserves U_K = [W_K,K]. The relative block calculation
identifies U_K with the moving subgroup generated by the smaller K-orbit of z;
consequently O₂(KTᵥ) fixes U_K.

One remaining action comparison is isolated: an element of Lᵥ fixing U_K
must fix W_K. If that holds, [O₂(KTᵥ),Lᵥ] fixes W_K. Thus the image of the
local two-core is normalized by both KTᵥ and Lᵥ, and is a normal two-group in
the larger reduced actor. It vanishes, giving the required local reducedness.
The last theorem is conditional on this Lᵥ kernel comparison, not a completed
source application. Its producer must use the genuine 13.6.11 movement and
the earlier cubic quotient of Lᵥ.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
B.2.13--14, printed p.78; 13.6.11--18, printed pp.928--931.
-/

@[expose] public section
open Subgroup Stellmacher
open scoped IsMulCommutative
open CFSG.Quasithin
open CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter13.Section06.CentralizerReduction
